  "subject": "🌿  Axios Finish Line: Reset rooms",
  "date": "Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:29:32 -0400",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🏔️ Plus: Peak views | Wednesday, September 30, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n PRESENTED BY COX ENTERPRISES \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Sep 30, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Welcome back! Smart Brevity™ count: 396 words … 1½ mins. Edited by Amy Stern. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: Take a pause \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Schools are giving overwhelmed kids a place to reset, Axios ' Natalie Daher writes .\n\n 🧠 Across the country, schools are adding calming rooms, \"Zen Dens\" and other supervised spaces where kids can step away for a few minutes, settle themselves and return to class. The idea is to ease stress before it leads to a meltdown, a trip to the principal's office or an absence from school. Why it matters: We spend a lot of time teaching children how to push through discomfort. Some schools are also teaching them when, and how, to pause.\n\n 🏫 Case in point: Nearly 20 Iowa schools had adopted \"brain health retreat rooms\" as of early this year, Axios Des Moines' Jason Clayworth reports .\n\n Up to five students can use a room for 10 minutes staffed with school social workers. At Ottumwa High, students made about 1,000 visits in the first half of last year. Officials say school attendance has improved since the rooms opened, while some students need them less as they build coping skills. Zoom out: Similar efforts are popping up elsewhere.\n\n The National Education Association reported in 2024 that schools were using staffed calming rooms to help students manage anger, anxiety and other difficult emotions before returning to class. At Hough High School , outside Charlotte, N.C., students who feel too stressed or anxious to focus can spend up to 15 minutes in a supervised \"Zen Den,\" with a counselor available if needed. The school says the goal is to build resilience and coping habits. 🔬 What the research says: There's good evidence for teaching kids self-regulation, even if research specifically on dedicated calming rooms is still limited.\n\n A JAMA Pediatrics review of 49 randomized trials involving more than 23,000 children and adolescents found self-regulation interventions were effective overall. Many studies have found improvements in academic achievement, social skills, mental health and behavior. ✨ The bottom line: Feeling overwhelmed doesn't have to derail the day. These rooms give kids a place to pause — and practice getting themselves back on track.\n\n Get Axios Local : Daily newsletters in 43 cities. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM COX ENTERPRISES\r\n\n \r\n Young people, big environmental impact \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Cox Conserves Heroes recognizes the volunteers and nonprofits helping the planet. \n\n\r\n The story: Previous finalist Ryan Hickman, now 17, started recycling at age 3 and has recycled over 1.6 million cans and bottles. \n\n\r\n Vote by Oct. 4 for your favorite and help them win up to $30,000.\n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. 🌍 Postcards from Eastern Europe \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: Kate Marino Axios executive editor Kate Marino sends us these spectacular views from a recent sabbatical spent across Eastern Europe — from the dramatic peaks of Montenegro's Prokletije Mountains to the shores of North Macedonia's Lake Ohrid.\n\n Photo: Kate Marino \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
