td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Take a pause </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/RGM7Ef1XXQ4bOWY8Du2pvQFKPn4=/0x0:1280x720/2026/09/28/1790613336277.gif\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Animated illustration of a sign with a shaking swearing emoji on it next to a classroom door. The emoji stops shaking, changes to an angry emoji, and then changes to a neutral emoji.\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>Schools are giving</strong> overwhelmed kids a place to reset, <em>Axios</em>' <em>Natalie Daher writes</em>.</p><ul><li>🧠 <strong>Across the country,</strong> schools are adding calming rooms, \"Zen Dens\" and other supervised spaces where kids can step away for a few minutes, settle themselves and return to class. </li><li><strong>The idea is to</strong> <strong>ease</strong> stress before it leads to a meltdown, a trip to the principal's office or an absence from school.<em> </em></li></ul><p><strong>Why it matters: </strong>We spend a lot of time teaching children how to push through discomfort. Some schools are also teaching them when, and how, to pause.</p><p>🏫 <strong>Case in point: </strong>Nearly 20 Iowa schools had adopted \"brain health retreat rooms\" as of early this year, <em>Axios Des Moines' Jason Clayworth <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47727079.270899/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL2xvY2FsL2Rlcy1tb2luZXMvMjAyNi8wOS8yMi9pb3dhLXNjaG9vbHMtYnJhaW4taGVhbHRoLXJldHJlYXQtcm9vbXM_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBbf3fa8d1\" target=\"_blank\">reports</a></em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47727079.270899/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL2xvY2FsL2Rlcy1tb2luZXMvMjAyNi8wOS8yMi9pb3dhLXNjaG9vbHMtYnJhaW4taGVhbHRoLXJldHJlYXQtcm9vbXM_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aCbf3fa8d1\" target=\"_blank\"></a>.</p><ul><li><strong>Up to five students</strong> can use a room for 10 minutes staffed with school social workers.</li><li><strong>At</strong> <strong>Ottumwa High,</strong> students made about 1,000 visits in the first half of last year. Officials say school<strong> </strong>attendance has improved since the rooms opened, while some students need them less as they build coping skills.</li></ul><p><strong>Zoom out:</strong> Similar efforts are popping up elsewhere.</p><ul><li><strong>The National Education Association</strong> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47727079.270899/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmVhLm9yZy9uZWEtdG9kYXkvYWxsLW5ld3MtYXJ0aWNsZXMvc2Nob29sLWNhbG1pbmctcm9vbXM_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB09436590\" target=\"_blank\">reported</a> in 2024 that schools were using staffed calming rooms to help students manage anger, anxiety and other difficult emotions before returning to class. </li><li><strong>At </strong><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47727079.270899/aHR0cHM6Ly9zaXRlcy5nb29nbGUuY29tL2Ntcy5rMTIubmMudXMvaG91Z2hzdHVkZW50c2VydmljZXMvemVuLWRlbj91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB2e5e5376\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Hough High School</strong></a><strong>,</strong> outside Charlotte, N.C., students who feel too stressed or anxious to focus can spend up to 15 minutes in a supervised \"Zen Den,\" with a counselor available if needed. The school says the goal is to build resilience and coping habits.</li></ul><p>🔬 <strong>What the research says:</strong> There's good evidence for teaching kids self-regulation, even if research specifically on dedicated calming rooms is still limited.</p><ul><li><strong>A </strong><strong><em>JAMA Pediatrics</em></strong><strong> </strong><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47727079.270899/aHR0cHM6Ly9qYW1hbmV0d29yay5jb20vam91cm5hbHMvamFtYXBlZGlhdHJpY3MvZnVsbGFydGljbGUvMjY3Nzg5OD91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBb3484acd\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>review</strong></a> of 49 randomized trials involving more than 23,000 children and adolescents found self-regulation interventions were effective overall. </li><li><strong>Many studies have found</strong> improvements in academic achievement, social skills, mental health and behavior.</li></ul><p>✨ <strong>The bottom line: </strong>Feeling overwhelmed doesn't have to derail the day. These rooms give kids a place to pause — and practice getting themselves back on track.</p><p><em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47727079.270899/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2xvY2FsP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB639731fd